    <briefdescription>
<para>Given that a condition must be able to evaluate to either false or to true, two conditions can be related in one of seven ways: </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para><itemizedlist>
<listitem>
<para><bold>Independent:</bold> <emphasis>(Unrelated)</emphasis> This condition is independent of that condition; <computeroutput><preformatted>
               this
               F   T
             +===+===+
           F | x │ x |
      that   +===+===+
           T | x │ x |
             +===+===+
     </preformatted></computeroutput> </para>
</listitem>
<listitem>
<para><bold>Equivalent:</bold> This condition is equivalent to that condition; <computeroutput><preformatted>
               this
               F   T
             +===+===+
           F | x │   |
      that   +===+===+
           T |   │ x |
             +===+===+
     </preformatted></computeroutput> </para>
</listitem>
<listitem>
<para><bold>Inverse:</bold> This condition is the inverse of that condition; <computeroutput><preformatted>
               this
               F   T
             +===+===+
           F |   │ x |
      that   +===+===+
           T | x │   |
             +===+===+
     </preformatted></computeroutput> </para>
</listitem>
<listitem>
<para><bold>Mutual-Exclusion:</bold> This condition is mutually exclusive with that condition; <computeroutput><preformatted>
               this
               F   T
             +===+===+
           F | x │ x |
      that   +===+===+
           T | x │   |
             +===+===+
     </preformatted></computeroutput> </para>
</listitem>
<listitem>
<para><bold>Mutual-Inclusion:</bold> This condition is mutually inclusive with that condition; <computeroutput><preformatted>
               this
               F   T
             +===+===+
           F |   │ x |
      that   +===+===+
           T | x │ x |
             +===+===+
     </preformatted></computeroutput> </para>
</listitem>
<listitem>
<para><bold>Implies:</bold> If this is true, it implies that is true; <computeroutput><preformatted>
               this
               F   T
             +===+===+
           F | x │   |
      that   +===+===+
           T | x │ x |
             +===+===+
     </preformatted></computeroutput> </para>
</listitem>
<listitem>
<para><bold>Implied:</bold> If that is true, this is implied to be true. <computeroutput><preformatted>
               this
               F   T
             +===+===+
           F | x │ x |
      that   +===+===+
           T |   │ x |
             +===+===+
     </preformatted></computeroutput> </para>
</listitem>
</itemizedlist>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
